   :migration-authorized false
   :reason "Two independent blockers, both verified against upstream source rather than assumed. (1) Application-profile capability gate: this is a langgraph.graph state-graph actor (intake->advise->govern->decide->commit/hold, human-approval interrupt, checkpointed) with an LLM-swappable advisor and a mutable-atom Store -- kotoba/app territory per orgs/kotoba-lang/kotoba/docs/lang/application-profile.md's completion gate (typed descriptors, effect inference/admission, policy-gated provider, positive/denial fixtures, quota/audit, 2-runtime parity). That gate has not passed for LLM/actor/state effects: the doc's own named proving slice, gftdcojp/ai-gftd-ghosthacker-shiropico, has migrated exactly one pure decision function (src/shiropico/publish_decision.kotoba) and still carries advisor.cljc/operation.cljc/phase.cljc/policy.cljc/render.cljc/store.cljc as CLJC -- the full state/LLM/actor loop is not yet capability-complete anywhere in the fleet, so no actor repository in this wave can have Kotoba as its sole production authority yet. (2) Even the pure sub-computation is not fully portable: mineralplant.governor/check's hard-violations includes a defense-in-depth free-text scope-exclusion check (case-folded substring search of the proposal rationale against ~11 finalization/execution phrases) alongside its closed-set op-allowlist check. orgs/kotoba-lang/compiler's frontend.cljc string-operations set is exactly {string-byte-length string=? string-concat string-replace-all keyword-from-string keyword-name} -- no substring search, no case-fold, no index-of. Porting only the op-allowlist half and dropping the phrase half would be a silent domain-narrowing of a safety-critical governor invariant, forbidden by this file's :policy. Extracting a governor pure-kernel is therefore blocked on the same string-search primitive gap independently of the application-profile gate."
