   :review-status :reviewed-2026-07-22
   :migration-authorized false
   :reason "Pure, GPU-free, capability-free little-endian columnar binary decoder (KAMI render-IR frame format: magic/version/column-header/payload parsing plus IEEE-754 binary16-to-f32 tint decoding) -- otherwise an excellent bounded-parser candidate matching the org-iso-h264/org-iso-isobmff precedent (both already qualified through the compiler's binary-input capability). Blocked on one missing primitive: rd-u16/rd-u32 byte assembly and f16->f32's exponent/mantissa extraction use `bit-shift-right`/`bit-or`, and orgs/kotoba-lang/compiler's frontend.cljc `arithmetic` set only admits `bit-and`/`bit-xor` (no shift, no or). The u16/u32/f16 bit-shift extractions are algebraically re-expressible via quot/mod (bit-shift-right h 10 == quot h 1024, bit-and x 0x1f == mod x 32, etc, since h is always a non-negative byte-derived value) -- this is a real, tractable path, just not implemented in this review pass."
